    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d60">

                <pb facs="0101" n="83" xml:id="pg83"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 Control (Germany)/4–2046</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister for Foreign Affairs of the Soviet
                        Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Molotov</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi><anchor n="15" xml:id="d60-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Translation]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Moscow</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-04-20">20 April, 1946</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I have your message concerning the desirability of exchanging views in regard to
                    the draft treaty for the disarmament of Germany.<anchor n="16" xml:id="d60-f2"/>
                    The draft of the treaty arouses serious objections. However, I will be prepared
                    to exchange views with you on this question in Paris.</p>
                <postscript>
                    <p>[Telegram 743, April 20, to Moscow, <ref target="frus:frus1946v05/pg_335"
                            >Volume V, page 335</ref>, asked that the Soviet Foreign Minister be
                        informed that the United States Government desired to discuss a treaty
                        concerning Austria at the forthcoming meeting of the Council of Foreign
                        Ministers. Telegram 1340, April 25, from Moscow, <ref
                            target="frus:frus1946v05/pg_336">Volume V, page 336</ref>, transmitted
                        the text of Foreign Minister Molotov’s letter of April 22 which stated that
                        the Soviet Government saw no possibility of discussing Austria at the
                        forthcoming Council meeting.]</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d60-f1" n="15" type="source" xml:id="d60-f1-content">
                <p>Transmitted to the Secretary by Soviet Ambassador Novikov on April 20, 1946.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d60-f2" n="16" xml:id="d60-f2-content">
                <p>The Secretary’s message to Molotov referred to here is quoted in telegram 708,
                    April 16, to Moscow, <ref target="#pg62">p. 62</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
